    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Verb always in the singular",
     "texto": [
      "In German «niemand» and «jemand» always take a singular verb: **Niemand weiß es** (nobody knows it), **Hat jemand angerufen?** (has anyone called?)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Contrast and declension",
     "texto": [
      "**Jemand** indicates an undetermined presence or existence; **niemand** expresses total absence. Optionally they take case endings in the accusative (**jemanden / niemanden**) and dative (**jemandem / niemandem**): **Ich habe niemanden gesehen**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
